# Project skill library synced from the global OpenCode skills dir
# (`npx skills add`); vendored third-party code, so kept out of git and
# paired with the matching eslint ignore in eslint.config.mjs.
# The backup folder holds the same vendored code, parked by
# `pnpm skills:prune --apply` before it is restored.
.opencode/skills/
.opencode/skills-backup/
.playwright-cli/

# Machine-local AI memory overlays — never commit (AGENTS.local.example.md)
AGENTS.local.md
AGENT.local.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.qoder/AGENTS.local.md
.kilo/AGENTS.local.md

# Local AI agent sessions/cache/state
.ai-cache/
.aider/
.kilo/plans/

# Local tool configs that may contain machine-specific paths
**/kilo.local.jsonc
**/*.local.md

# Agent tool mirrors — generated by `pnpm agent:sync --write`, never commit.
# The canonical agent and command files are `.opencode/agents/` and
# `.opencode/commands/` (see agents.registry.json → sources.canonical); every
# directory below holds the per-tool copies each AI client reads locally.
.augment/
.claude/
.cline/
.codex/
.continue/
.cursor/
.gemini/
.kilocode/
.roo/
.trae/
.windsurf/
# These four also carry tracked content (.kilo/.qoder rules adapters,
# .kiro/skills and .github/workflows), so only their generated mirror
# subdirectories are ignored.
.kilo/agents/
.kilo/commands/
.qoder/agents/
.qoder/commands/
.kiro/agents/
.kiro/commands/
.github/prompts/

# uv-managed Python environments (hash-named install dirs)
b5bf2e54cb654f7b/

# brainstorming visual companion session artifacts
.superpowers/
